IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `eia-core-interpretation`
IMPORT `ei6-part-9-coming-into-force`
IMPORT `ei6-part-9-transitional`

-- Tests of ei6-part-9-transitional (Act ss 156 to 165, src:3105-3151). Expected values are read from the text by hand.
-- The former Act is repealed on June 30, 1996, the day s 190(1) fixes, at the start of that day (fork F-ei6-14).

§ `Repealed provisions`

#ASSERT count (`ss 158, 159(5), 162 and 166 - repealed, and therefore not encoded`) EQUALS 4

§ `Sections 156 and 157`

#ASSERT `s 156 the training allowance may continue to be paid in accordance with the National Training Act` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 156 the training allowance may continue to be paid in accordance with the National Training Act` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 156 the training allowance may continue to be paid in accordance with the National Training Act` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 157 the agreement continues in effect according to its terms` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 157 the agreement continues in effect according to its terms` FALSE)

§ `Section 159 - the former Act`

#ASSERT `s 159 the day on which the former Act is repealed` EQUALS YearMonthDay 1996 6 30
-- (1): a benefit period beginning before the repeal is dealt with under the former Act (src:3112).
#ASSERT `s 159(1) the Act under which matters relating to the claim are dealt with` (YearMonthDay 1996 6 29) EQUALS `ei6 the former Act (the Unemployment Insurance Act)`
#ASSERT `s 159(1) the Act under which matters relating to the claim are dealt with` (YearMonthDay 1996 6 30) EQUALS `ei6 this Act`
#ASSERT `s 159(1) the Act under which matters relating to the claim are dealt with` (YearMonthDay 1997 2 2) EQUALS `ei6 this Act`
-- (1.01): the Tax Court of Canada need not give reasons in writing, but may (src:3114).
#ASSERT `s 159(1.01) the Tax Court of Canada need not give reasons in writing for its decision` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 159(1.01) the Tax Court of Canada need not give reasons in writing for its decision` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 159(1.01) the Tax Court of Canada may give reasons in writing for its decision` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 159(1.01) the Tax Court of Canada may give reasons in writing for its decision` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 159(1.01) the Tax Court of Canada may give reasons in writing for its decision` FALSE TRUE)
-- (1.1): subsection 19(3) applies to a period beginning on or after January 5, 1997; deductions on or after that day for
-- a period beginning after June 30, 1996 (src:3116). A period beginning on June 30, 1996 itself is not "after" it, though
-- section 190(3.2) says "on or after": the two differ on that one day (finding in NOTES.md).
#ASSERT NOT (`s 159(1.1) subsection 19(3) applies to the claimant` (YearMonthDay 1997 1 4))
#ASSERT `s 159(1.1) subsection 19(3) applies to the claimant` (YearMonthDay 1997 1 5)
#ASSERT `s 159(1.1) the Commission may make a deduction under subparagraph 19(3)(a)(i)` (YearMonthDay 1997 1 5) (YearMonthDay 1996 7 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 159(1.1) the Commission may make a deduction under subparagraph 19(3)(a)(i)` (YearMonthDay 1997 1 4) (YearMonthDay 1996 7 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 159(1.1) the Commission may make a deduction under subparagraph 19(3)(a)(i)` (YearMonthDay 1997 1 5) (YearMonthDay 1996 6 30))
#ASSERT `s 190(3.2) the Commission may make a deduction under subparagraph 19(3)(a)(i)` (YearMonthDay 1997 1 5) (YearMonthDay 1996 6 30)
-- (1.2), (2) and (6): after the repeal, which is the start of June 30, 1996.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 159(1.2) subsection 19(4) applies to the claimant` (YearMonthDay 1996 6 29))
#ASSERT `s 159(1.2) subsection 19(4) applies to the claimant` (YearMonthDay 1996 6 30)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 159(2) section 23 applies in place of section 20 of the former Act` (YearMonthDay 1996 6 29))
#ASSERT `s 159(2) section 23 applies in place of section 20 of the former Act` (YearMonthDay 1996 7 15)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 159(6) sections 27 to 33 apply in place of sections 27 to 28.3 of the former Act` (YearMonthDay 1996 6 29))
#ASSERT `s 159(6) sections 27 to 33 apply in place of sections 27 to 28.3 of the former Act` (YearMonthDay 1996 6 30)
-- (3), (4): section 25 and section 26 of the former Act apply only to claimants already in the project or course.
#ASSERT `s 159(3) section 25 of the former Act applies to the claimant` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 159(3) section 25 of the former Act applies to the claimant` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 159(4) section 26 of the former Act applies to the claimant` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 159(4) section 26 of the former Act applies to the claimant` FALSE)
-- (6): a reference in the former Act to section 27, 28, 28.1, 28.2 or 28.3 (src:3128-3132).
#ASSERT `s 159(6) the section of this Act that a reference in the former Act is read as a reference to` 27 EQUALS JUST 27
#ASSERT `s 159(6) the section of this Act that a reference in the former Act is read as a reference to` 28 EQUALS JUST 29
#ASSERT `s 159(6) the section of this Act that a reference in the former Act is read as a reference to` 28.1 EQUALS JUST 31
#ASSERT `s 159(6) the section of this Act that a reference in the former Act is read as a reference to` 28.2 EQUALS JUST 32
#ASSERT `s 159(6) the section of this Act that a reference in the former Act is read as a reference to` 28.3 EQUALS JUST 33
#ASSERT `s 159(6) the section of this Act that a reference in the former Act is read as a reference to` 29 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (7): section 145 applies in place of section 123 for benefits paid after December 31, 1995 (src:3134).
#ASSERT NOT (`s 159(7) section 145 applies in place of section 123 of the former Act` (YearMonthDay 1995 12 31))
#ASSERT `s 159(7) section 145 applies in place of section 123 of the former Act` (YearMonthDay 1996 1 1)

§ `Sections 160 and 161`

-- 160: before June 30, 1996 the former Act; on or after June 30, 1996 and before January 5, 1997 this Act as it applies on
-- June 30, 1996; Part VIII and later days are not covered (src:3136-3138).
#ASSERT `s 160 the law that determines the hours of insurable employment and the insurable earnings` `Part I` (YearMonthDay 1996 6 29) EQUALS JUST `ei6 the former Act`
#ASSERT `s 160 the law that determines the hours of insurable employment and the insurable earnings` `Part I` (YearMonthDay 1996 6 30) EQUALS JUST `ei6 this Act as it applies on June 30, 1996`
#ASSERT `s 160 the law that determines the hours of insurable employment and the insurable earnings` `Part I` (YearMonthDay 1997 1 4) EQUALS JUST `ei6 this Act as it applies on June 30, 1996`
#ASSERT `s 160 the law that determines the hours of insurable employment and the insurable earnings` `Part I` (YearMonthDay 1997 1 5) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 160 the law that determines the hours of insurable employment and the insurable earnings` `Part VIII` (YearMonthDay 1996 6 29) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 161 the matter is dealt with under the former Act` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 161 the matter is dealt with under the former Act` FALSE)

§ `Sections 163 and 165`

#ASSERT `s 163(1) the Commission's estimate of the insurable earnings of all insured persons in the fiscal year 1996-97 must be published in the Canada Gazette` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 163(1) the Commission's estimate of the insurable earnings of all insured persons in the fiscal year 1996-97 must be published in the Canada Gazette` TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 163(2) the plan mentioned in section 79 for the fiscal year 1996-97 must be published in the Canada Gazette` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 163(2) the plan mentioned in section 79 for the fiscal year 1996-97 must be published in the Canada Gazette` TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 165 the waiver or agreement continues in effect as though made under paragraph 5(4)(d) of this Act` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 165 the waiver or agreement continues in effect as though made under paragraph 5(4)(d) of this Act` FALSE)
